  "paint-splash: rating 6.5 out of 10, below the bar of 7.0 ... reads as a scalloped badge, not
  wet paint; ring seams on the face; a foot tab on both faces; one flat mid-value".
Scope: assets/paint-splash.ts and its brief. No other asset, no file in src/ and no script
  changed. The two checker files of the finding were added to the repository unchanged.

## The five changes, in the order the task gave them

1. The foot is 0.02 m deep, not 0.04 m. The paint is 0.025 m thick at the rim, so the foot now
   sits inside the thickness of the blob and shows no tab in front of or behind the faces. The
   width stays 0.06 m and the height stays 0.02 m.
2. Every lobe, drop and neck joins the disc with one smoothUnion of k 0.025 m. The old joins used
   k 0.004 m for the lobes and k 0.01 m for the drops, and each left a ring on the face. The
   lobes and the drops are soft domes now, so the face carries no ring seam.
3. The faces curve. A dome ellipsoid lifts the centre of the blob 0.008 m above the rim: 0.033 m
   thick at the centre, 0.025 m at the rim. The roughness is 0.25, so the paint reads wet.
4. The outer 0.015 m of the outline is painted 25 % darker than the paint colour, through the
   `paint` slot (k.tint('paint', -0.25)). The band follows the silhouette on the front face, the
   back face and the rim. A preset recolours the whole slot, so each preset keeps its own dark rim.
5. The splash keeps 0.30 m across, stands on y = 0, faces +Z, and holds under 8,000 triangles.

The dark band is cut from the footprint of the outline: the same outline, made tall, so its shell
keeps the front face, the back face and the rim. The band measures 0.015 m (probed at 0.000 m at
15 mm inside the silhouette and -0.005 m at the foot).

