## Notes for the reviewer

- The built splash measures 0.291 x 0.252 x 0.05 m and holds 1,968 triangles in the textured build
  (out/paint-splash/stats.json). The bottom sits at y = -0.001 m. The paint is 0.025 m thick at the
  rim and 0.033 m at the centre; the wide fillet adds about 7 mm at the lobe joins, so the
  bounding box is 0.05 m deep.
- The mean colour of the front cutout is #e74f45. The old build read #f3635c, a pale coral. The
  three preset cutouts read #e74f45 (red), #487fbf (blue) and #f0c447 (yellow).
- The dark rim is a soft deeper edge, not a hard outline: the studio light lifts the rim, so the
  mean of the outer band is #e04e44 against #f15147 inside it. The centre stays mid-value, because
  the order put the darker paint only on the outer 0.015 m. `forge inspect` still warns that almost
  everything is mid-value.
- The three droplets now read as round bumps on the rim. The fillet of 0.025 m swallows a 0.01 m
  neck, so the brief's thin necks are gone. The maker followed the order and did not choose a
  different fillet.

## The open design questions for the orchestrator

- The three droplets keep no thin neck. A smaller fillet on the necks alone, or a longer neck,
  would keep them. The order fixed one fillet for the lobes, the drops and the necks.
- The foot lies inside the dark band, so the foot is dark. A band cut from the outline without the
  foot would leave the foot in the mid-value.
- The centre of the splash stays mid-value. A darker centre needs another value than the order
  gave.
- The cutout command takes --preset, so the blue and yellow cutouts exist. The stage prop field of
  the acceptance finding N3 stays open for the owner of the song stage files.

- out/ is not tracked. The committed paths are assets/paint-splash.ts, the brief, the two checker
  files of the finding, the plan sub-bullet and this log.
- The maker does not rate its own work.

